Menu: take input from every SimpleTextIn, not just ConIn (physical keys)

Mechanism
---------
The UniXNU menu loop (UniXNUMenuRun) and the confirmation prompt
(UniXNUMenuConfirm) wait on gST->ConIn->WaitForKey and read from
gST->ConIn only. On the Qualcomm Mu platforms this firmware targets,
the console splitter never aggregates ButtonsDxe: that driver installs
EFI_SIMPLE_TEXT_INPUT_PROTOCOL on its own handle to serve the
MsButtonServices front page, so its keys exist in the system but can
never reach ConIn. On flashlm this left the menu with no working
input at all (touch and buttons both dead; only the countdown and the
fallback-retry patch kept the board usable).

Fix: enumerate every SimpleTextIn instance once per menu run
(LocateHandleBuffer by protocol) and treat them all as the menu's
keyboard -- the main loop adds every instance's WaitForKey to the
existing WaitForEvent set next to the periodic timer and reads the key
from whichever instance signaled; the confirmation prompt drains and
waits across the same set via a shared helper. The splitter handle
carries the protocol too, so ConIn is simply one entry of the list
and is not special-cased (it is re-added explicitly only if the
enumeration somehow finds nothing).

No key translation is added: ButtonsDxe already emits exactly the
codes the existing key switch consumes (stock flashlmdd binary,
ButtonsLib key translation: volume up -> SCAN_UP, volume down ->
SCAN_DOWN, power -> SCAN_SUSPEND; UnicodeChar 0 in all three cases).

Deviation from upstream
-----------------------
Upstream UniXNU reads gST->ConIn exclusively in Menu.c. This patch
changes only how input is sourced inside the two input functions of
Menu.c; menu rendering, the countdown/fallback-retry semantics, the
HasInput/rotation rules and the set of accepted keys are untouched.
With no key pressed the behaviour is identical to before (waiting is
still purely event driven, no polling is introduced).

Applies on top of the current build-tree Menu.c (which already carries
menu-fallback-retry.patch). Baseline Menu.c MD5:
5c0f0322ce0fc3a52aee9d5850225509

